{
  "_source": "https://stratswiki.com/sos-fomt/events/villager-events/ (anna, dudley, lou) plus https://ranchstory.miraheze.org/wiki/Events_(Story_of_Seasons:_Friends_of_Mineral_Town) (rival events) plus direct game knowledge for two entries",
  "_note": "Static wiki reference data for the planned Reminders feature -- one-off/recurring villager events that aren't seasonal Festivals (see festivals.json for those) or a marriage candidate's own colored Heart Event sequence (see heart_events.json for those). Not memory-derived. Structured (including a Rival Events pass) to structure every date/season/weather/FP gate the SAME WAY heart_events.json's own gates work, field-for-field, so both tables read consistently: 'days_mode' ('any'/'only'/'exclude') + 'days' (a list of weekday names, meaningful only when days_mode isn't 'any') -- identical semantics to heart_events.json's own days_mode/days. 'season_mode' ('any'/'only'/'exclude') + 'season' -- identical to heart_events.json. 'other_villager_fp_min' equivalent here is 'villager_fp_min' (a list of {villager_name,min_fp}, ALL listed villagers' live Friendship (+0x10) must be at or above min_fp) -- same field shape/helper as heart_events.json's gate, renamed since an other_event doesn't have a single 'subject' villager the way a heart event does (some, like Rick and Karen's Rival Events, gate on TWO villagers at once). 'requires_met' (a list of villager names, ALL must have the live 'met at least once' flag +0x1B set) -- identical to heart_events.json. Two fields this table needed that heart_events.json never did: 'year_mode' ('any'/'only'/'min') + 'year' -- parallels season_mode's shape for a Year-N-only or Year-N-or-later restriction; and 'day_of_month'/'day_of_month_range' -- an exact day-of-month (Mayor Thomas' Day 2) or an inclusive [min,max] day-of-month range (Harvest Goddess High & Low's Days 1-5), for events keyed to the calendar rather than a weekday. 'villager_lp_max' (a list of {villager_name,max_lp}, ALL listed villagers' live Love Points must be BELOW max_lp) is the mirror image of villager_fp_min, needed for Rival Events which only fire while the player's own heart level with both rival-pair villagers is still low (data/tables/heart_levels.json's tier minimums, e.g. 'less than Purple Heart' = LP < 10000). 'villager_lp_min' (a list of {villager_name,min_lp}) is villager_lp_max's own mirror image in turn -- a MINIMUM LP gate, needed for e.g. Elly's Medical Study (Purple Heart or higher with both Elly and Doctor). 'weather' (null, or a list of allowed WEATHER_NAMES strings, OR'd together -- e.g. ['Rainy','Snowy']) stays as its own field rather than heart_events.json's boolean Sunny-only 'weather_required', since this table has real Rain-or-Snow cases that a boolean can't express. All gate fields default to 'any'/null/[] when unused. 'requirements' is pure DISPLAY-ONLY caveat text for whatever still can't be live-checked (an NPC's own presence, a marriage-exclusivity note, etc.) -- empty string means nothing left to show. 'url' is null for the one entry with no dedicated wiki event page (Tasty Time TV Show -- Mayor Thomas' Annual Request instead links a related item page, see its own entry); Ran's Mother's Memorial Day and Dudley and Duke's Fight share Dudley's stratswiki villager-events page since that wiki documents both events there together; Rick and Karen's Rival Event entries point at the miraheze events page (no dedicated per-event wiki page exists). Van's Shop and Van's Pet Shop were removed from this table -- both are already fully modeled by the Shop Info section (data/tables/shops.json, incl. Van's Pet Shop's own day-15 special rule), so listing them here too was pure duplication; Shop Info's own _SHOPS_EXCLUDED_FROM_SHOP_INFO workaround (which existed only to avoid double-showing these two) was removed at the same time. Rival Events (miraheze page) are two-NPC storylines (e.g. Rick and Karen, Kai and Popuri) gated on the PLAYER's own heart level with both staying below a threshold. Every event on the miraheze events page has been reviewed (all 5 Rival Event pairs, every Townsfolk villager Anna through Mugi) except FOUR deliberately excluded categories: Harvest Goddess's own milestone events (A Heavenly Introduction, An Investment's Return, For the Goddess, A Rare Gift, The Goddess's Collection, Spring Mine Milestones, The Goddess' Treasure) and Kappa's Offering events (1st/10th cucumber offering, daily offering, Get Kappa's Treasure, Kappa Disaster) -- both trigger off cumulative counts/floors reached, not calendar/weather, so they don't fit this table's model at all (Hidden Counters already covers the Harvest Goddess offering-count side); Huang's 6 shop events (Gold thresholds, item ownership, and two actual minigames) -- more complex gating than this table's schema supports, revisit separately if wanted; and Nature Sprites' Tea Party -- explicitly declined: it can fire multiple times, is random, and the game already mails the player a letter when it happens, so a reminder is redundant. Every entry gets a manual Show/Completed toggle via app/event_settings.py's Event Settings dialog -- Completed hides an event even while its live conditions still match, since most of this table (unlike heart_events.json's LP-counter-backed colored events) has no live 'already happened' flag; Show lets an inapplicable one (e.g. Bon Vivant's Lunch/Dinner if not married to Bon Vivant) be hidden outright. A handful of entries (Cliff Collapses Part 2, In Need of Advice 2, Equine Evaluation) fire a fixed number of days after ANOTHER event in this table with no live way to track that offset -- these gate on every other live condition (FP/weather/year/season) but not the day count itself, and lean on the Completed checkbox once the event has actually been seen.",
